From df74f5e244f835e63cebb2e32754d5a4fe2f8a02 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude (review)" <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 12:49:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] robustness: check every allocation, read and file open

pulsar_det_an_v4.c

  The bulk data load did none of its checks. malloc of the whole
  selected range (gigabytes for a long observation) was dereferenced
  without testing for NULL, and the fread return value was discarded -
  the one warning the existing Makefile flags already emitted.

  The discarded fread is the more dangerous of the two. If the input
  file is shorter than the requested section range, the tail of the
  buffer is uninitialised memory which the fold loop sums into comprs
  as though it were data. The run completes and prints a plausible SNR
  computed partly from garbage. It is now a clear error naming the
  shortfall. The cutdat.bin write is checked too, so a full disk is
  reported rather than producing a truncated copy.

  bestprof is now zero-initialised. It is printed unconditionally into
  profile.txt column 3, but only assigned inside a branch that never
  fires if every SNR in the rolling window is non-positive.

io/files.c

  None of the 32 output file opens were checked. A non-writable working
  directory meant the first fprintf to a NULL handle segfaulted after
  the banner had printed, which looks like a crash inside the analysis
  rather than a permissions problem.

  The table is now calloc'd, since the loop skips the two attenuation
  slots and left them holding uninitialised heap, and close_files skips
  NULL handles rather than calling fclose on them.

  open_files() is declared (void) so the compiler checks its callers.

pulsar_det_an_v4.c and io/files.c now build warning-free under
-Wall -Wextra -Wpedantic.

Verified byte-identical: all 37 output files match the baseline.
---
 RTL/bin/Blankf.txt         |  1 -
 RTL/bin/Blanks.txt         |  1 -
 RTL/includes/io/files.h    |  2 +-
 RTL/src/io/files.c         | 30 +++++++++++++++++++----
 RTL/src/pulsar_det_an_v4.c | 49 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 5 files changed, 71 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

